# `references/` holds git submodules (the PM spec repo and the chat-kit prototype) kept purely as
# background material — nothing in there is built, tested or linted by this workspace.
#
# They ship their own `vite.config.ts` / `package.json`, and `references/asgard-sdk-pm` nests a second
# copy of the prototype at `prototype/asgard-chat-kit-prototype`. Once `git submodule update --init
# --recursive` checks those out, Nx's `@nx/vite` plugin tries to load their configs, fails to resolve
# dependencies that were never installed here, and the whole project graph dies — taking every nx
# target with it, including `build:core` / `build:react`.
#
# The leading slash anchors this to the workspace root. Unanchored, gitignore semantics match a
# directory of that name at *any* depth, which would also swallow the shipped
# `packages/react/src/components/templates/references/` component — hiding it from `nx affected`,
# from lint, and from build-cache invalidation.
/references
